MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The test leads, resistor assortment, and heat shrink tubing support the small circuits I build with breadboards, LEDs, and a relay module by helping me connect, complete, and insulate them.",
    "The component tester feels useful because it would help me identify and check parts for those projects, and assembling it is appealing in its own right."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Printer filament, acrylic cement, and layout fluid require specific equipment, materials, or tasks that my purchases have not established a need for.",
    "The tap kit requires a particular thread size I have no current reason to use. The transistor assortment fits my interests, but 840 pieces is more than I would choose without a concrete circuit in mind."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in practical projects seems to have been stretched into an assumed need for supplies across printing, machining, and plastic assembly.",
    "An interest in electronics supplies seems to have been treated as a reason to buy more boards or large component assortments, regardless of what I already have or need."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Supplies that help me use the breadboards, LEDs, and relay module I already own feel more relevant than supplies that require starting a different kind of project.",
    "I already bought a PCB assortment, so more boards depend on my remaining supply. Quantities and exact specifications also matter because I tend to buy when a project gives me a clear reason."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my circuit-building interests but sometimes stretch them into unrelated project needs or quantities I cannot currently justify."
}
